From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmtksdio: wait out the MT7668 Wi-Fi firmware
 load

The MT7668S is a combo part: one patch serves both functions, and
whichever driver loads first downloads it. When the Wi-Fi driver does,
it goes on to load its own ram code for about 0.9 s, and Bluetooth
enabled in that window stops answering: setup sees the patch done, then
the low power command times out, and every later attempt fails the same
way until the part is reset.

When the patch is already there, wait for the Wi-Fi load to finish
before enabling Bluetooth. With the Wi-Fi driver forced to load first,
Bluetooth comes up 6 times of 6, against 0 of 10 without.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
  drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c |    8 ++++++++
  1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
@@ -800,6 +800,9 @@
 	return status;
 }
 
+/* the Wi-Fi ram code loads in about 0.9 s after the patch */
+#define MT7668_WIFI_LOAD_MS	2000
+
 static int mt76xx_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev, const char *fwname)
 {
 	struct btmtksdio_dev *bdev = hci_get_drvdata(hdev);
@@ -824,6 +827,11 @@
 
 	if (status == BTMTK_WMT_PATCH_DONE) {
 		bt_dev_info(hdev, "Firmware already downloaded");
+		/* by the MT7668's Wi-Fi function, which loads its own ram code
+		 * next; Bluetooth enabled meanwhile stops answering
+		 */
+		if (bdev->data->chipid == 0x7668)
+			msleep(MT7668_WIFI_LOAD_MS);
 		goto ignore_setup_fw;
 	}
 
